{
  "_read_floor_rules": [
    "Read rules ONLY. Per the Claude Code permissions docs, file permission checks match only Edit(path) and Read(path). A Grep(path) or Glob(path) rule is ACCEPTED BUT NEVER MATCHED and emits a startup warning for every such rule. Read rules are instead applied best-effort to the file-reading tools (Grep, Glob, @file mentions, IDE context), so Read(...) IS how you cover them. Never add Grep(...) or Glob(...) path rules here.",
    "ANCHORING: a bare/relative pattern like Read(**/.env) matches only at or under the CURRENT directory - it does NOT match a parent. Safe mode launches in a fresh throwaway workspace, so ~/.zshrc is always in a parent and a relative rule protects nothing. Anything outside the workspace MUST use ~/x (home-relative) or //x (filesystem root). //**/x matches anywhere on the filesystem.",
    "NOT COVERED by this profile, by design: Bash(ls:*) enumerates any directory (ls is an unconfigurable read-only builtin), Task spawns subagents, WebSearch is an outbound channel. Read/Edit denies also do not apply to subprocesses that open files themselves. For real containment use a low-privilege OS user or the sandbox."
  ],
  "permissions": {
    "defaultMode": "default",
    "allow": [
      "Read", "Grep", "Glob", "TodoWrite", "Task", "WebSearch",
      "Bash(ls:*)", "Bash(pwd)", "Bash(which:*)", "Bash(git status:*)"
